==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Relic Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Relic Doge Base]].
*1 [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*2 [[Midnite D.|Midnite Ds]] spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 120~126.67 seconds<sup>3,600f~3,800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*1 [[Midnite D.]] spawns after 73.33 seconds<sup>2,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Director Kurosawah]] spawns after 106.67 seconds<sup>3,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Midnite D.]] spawns after 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
A very money-tight stage. Midnite D. is a remarkably bulky adversary, with his many knockbacks letting your cats enter the range of Nyandam and Kurosawah. The silver lining is that the Doge Darks provide plenty of cash for you to deploy attackers. Midnite D.'s [[Shield]] doesn't have enough health for most [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercers]] to be worth it, so your best bet is to invest in cheap and effective units like [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]].

[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] is a surprisingly good option here, standing at a safe range and taking out a large chunk of a Midnite D.'s health to prevent several Shields from needing to be broken.

Once all Midnite Ds are defeated, the stage is effectively won, though treading past Nyandam and Kurosawah can be a long and tedious journey. [[Cat God the Great (Special Cat)|Cat God the Awesome]] and [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] can make this a lot easier.

==Trivia==
*Fire Kingdom Dynamite's Japanese name, Hi no Kuni Dai-Namaito (火の国ダイ=ナマイト, "Fire Nation Dai-Namite"), may be a pun on 大 ''dai'' (great; large) and ダイナマイト ''dainamaito'' (dynamite).
*Prior to [[Version 15.3 Update|Version 15.3]], the stage width was set to 4,900. The change was made because of a bug in how [[:Category:Animated Enemy Bases|Animated Bases]] spawn when not set as bosses.

